invariant: INV-38
file: tls.c
catches: test/handshake_sequence_shards.sh ./bin/handshake_sequence_test
builds: bin/handshake_sequence_test
reason: ch_read fails every record that io_read_record refuses with
  decode_error, so a peer that sends a header of 2^14 + 257 bytes after
  the handshake gets decode_error and not the record_overflow RFC 9846
  §5.2 requires. The sequence test's SEFA case under MUT_REC_HUGE reads
  the alert on the wire.

--- old
        tlsi_fail(t, alert);
        return rc;
    }
    if (outer != REC_APPDATA) {
--- new
        tlsi_fail(t, ALERT_DECODE_ERROR);
        return rc;
    }
    if (outer != REC_APPDATA) {
